research-pipeline
=================

Concept-ports from gpt-researcher — https://github.com/assafelovic/gpt-researcher
Copyright (c) Assaf Elovic, Apache License 2.0

No code was copied. gpt-researcher is a Python/FastAPI/LangGraph runtime with a
NextJS frontend; it is not vendored, and it is not a dependency. Two of its
design ideas were re-expressed for Cowork's primitives in our own words:

  - skills/literature-discovery/references/deep-research-loop.md
      The recursive deep-research shape: breadth/depth/concurrency
      parameterization, and propagating each level's learnings into the next
      level's queries rather than re-searching the root topic. The three-bucket
      digest schema, dry-branch termination, and the declared-budget gate are
      ours.

  - skills/research-evaluator/SKILL.md
      Scoring a generated report against the sources it actually retrieved, and
      recording cost and latency alongside quality (their evals/ suites). The
      claim-level grading rubric, the model-diverse judging, and the
      read-only-reporter posture are ours.

Per DR-011's folding heuristic: a native runtime with heavy overlap against a
shipped plugin is concept-ported, never vendored and never allowed to coexist.
